          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %em Calabi-Yau variety
            is an
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifold"} Kähler manifold
            with (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundle"}> holomorphically
            , rather than just topologically) trivial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian manifold
            of even
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 N
            which has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+holonomy"} special holonomy
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mi N
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(N)\subset O(2 N, \mathbb{R})
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+topological+space"} compact
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+manifolds"} Kähler manifolds
            %span.newWikiWord
              Yau's theorem
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Yau%27s+theorem"} ?
            (also known as the
            = succeed ")" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Calabi conjecture
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Calabi+conjecture"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
          %p
            Note that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1(X) = 0
            implies in general that the canonical bundle is
            = succeed "." do
              %em topologically trivial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a simply connected compact Kähler manifold,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1(X) = 0
            implies further that the canonical bundle is
            = succeed "." do
              %em holomorphically trivial
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A Calabi-Yau variety can be described algebraically as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+scheme"} proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety"} variety
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            (not necessarily
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed
            and not necessarily of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_X=\wedge^n\Omega^1\simeq \mathcal{O}_X
            and also
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^j(X, \mathcal{O}_X)=0
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi j
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\leq j \leq n-1
          %p
            If the base field is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and obtain a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            that satisfies the first given definition.
          %p
            Beware that there are slightly different (and inequivalent) definitions in use. Notably in some contexts only the trivialization of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+bundle"} canonical bundle
            is required, but not the vanishing of the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
